  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city of Venice is built on more than 100 small islands in the marshy lagoon along the Adriatic Sea. The canals, which are up to 10 meters deep, have been the lifeblood of the city for centuries. They provided a means of transportation and allowed the city to grow into the thriving commercial center it became during the Middle Ages.\n\nToday, Venice is still famous for its beautiful canals, ornate bridges, and stunning St Mark's Square. However, the city faces many challenges due to its unique environment. Rising sea levels and increased flooding are causing concern among residents and tourists alike. In recent years, the city has implemented various measures to protect itself from these threats, including the construction of a new floodgate system.\n\nDespite these efforts, some critics argue that Venice is becoming too reliant on tourism and that this is having a negative impact on the city's culture and way of life. They claim that the large number of visitors is causing overcrowding, pollution, and strain on local resources. Others counter that tourism brings in much-needed revenue and helps to preserve the city's rich history and architecture.\n\nThe future of Venice remains uncertain as it continues to navigate these complex issues. One thing is clear, however: the city will always be a source of fascination for those who visit or live there.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main reason why Venice has been built on more than 100 small islands?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Because it was founded by a group of wealthy merchants\", \"Due to its unique location in the marshy lagoon along the Adriatic Sea\", \"To provide a means of transportation for the city's inhabitants\", \"As part of a larger plan to create a new commercial center\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Due to its unique location in the marshy lagoon along the Adriatic Sea\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is one of the main challenges facing Venice today?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Rising sea levels and increased flooding\", \"Overcrowding and pollution caused by tourism\", \"Strain on local resources due to large numbers of visitors\", \"A lack of funding for preservation efforts\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Rising sea levels and increased flooding\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author mean by 'the city's culture and way of life'?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The city's rich history and architecture\", \"The local cuisine and traditional festivals\", \"The daily routines and customs of the residents\", \"The economic and commercial activities of the city\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The daily routines and customs of the residents\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards tourism in Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They strongly oppose it, citing its negative impact on the city\", \"They are neutral, seeing both positive and negative effects\", \"They believe it brings much-needed revenue and helps preserve the city's history\", \"They think it has no significant impact on the city\"],\n      \"answer\": \"They believe it brings much-needed revenue and helps preserve the city's history\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the future of Venice from the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It will continue to thrive as a commercial center\", \"It will become an even more popular tourist destination\", \"Its unique environment and cultural heritage will ensure its survival\", \"Its future remains uncertain due to various challenges\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Its future remains uncertain due to various challenges\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
